18:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","className":"min-h-screen bg-bg pt-24 pb-16","children":["$","article",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-2","children":"B2B SaaS Conversion"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"heading-1 text-fg md:text-5xl","children":"Run a Free SaaS Landing Page Audit to Boost Demo Conversions"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl","children":"B2B SaaS landing pages fail in specific, repeatable ways. Feature jargon where the ICP statement belongs. A demo CTA on a product that should offer a trial. No product UI above the fold. This guide covers each pattern with observable evidence and a bounded fix."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-stretch sm:items-center gap-3","children":[["$","$L1f",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=saas-audit-hero&utm_medium=hero-cta","className":"inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center justify-center rounded bg-accent px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-bg transition-opacity hover:opacity-85","children":"Get your free audit →"}],["$","$L1f",null,{"href":"/repair-sprint","className":"inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center justify-center rounded border border-border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-fg-muted transition-colors hover:border-fg-muted hover:text-fg","children":"Explore $97 Repair Sprint"}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg mb-6","children":"Six SaaS-specific conversion failures"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 mb-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mt-0.5","children":"01"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-0.5","children":"Headline (H1)"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold text-fg","children":"ICP statement replaced by category description"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-3 pl-7","children":"SaaS H1s typically describe the product category instead of naming who it is for. \"The all-in-one workspace\" tells a visitor nothing about whether they belong on the page. Cold paid traffic arriving from a targeted ad needs confirmation within the first viewport that the product matches their situation - not a feature description."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"pl-7 border-l-2 border-accent/30 ml-7","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wider mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Replace the product category with the buyer's situation. Who is this for, and what does it solve for them specifically? One sentence. Test against the ad headline to confirm message continuity."}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 mb-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mt-0.5","children":"02"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-0.5","children":"CTA"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold text-fg","children":"Demo CTA on a self-serve product"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6 mb-3 pl-7","children":"A demo CTA routes cold traffic into a sales pipeline. That is appropriate for products requiring implementation, procurement, or admin setup. For products below ~$200/month ACV that onboard in minutes, asking for a demo is a commitment mismatch - visitors who could convert in 2 minutes are instead put in a queue for a call. Webflow, Notion, and Calendly all have self-serve products. Their CTAs are correct. SaaS pages with comparable products that default to \"Book a demo\" are converting their most decisive visitors into waiting leads."}],"$L28"]}],"$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c"]}]]}],"$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31"]}]}]
